    "description": "As Ops, I want link changes recorded in assignment history, so I can see which link a rep ran during any period.\n\n* New fields on Deal_Rep_Assignment_History\\__c: Deal_Linkc (lookup), Previous_Deal_Linkc (lookup), Link_Code_Snapshotc Text(255), Event_Type_\\_c picklist (Created / Status Changed / Link Changed / Status + Link Changed)\n\n* THE EXISTING HISTORY AUTOMATION FIRES ON STATUS CHANGE ONLY and must be revised to fire on link change as well, with Event_Type__c set correctly for each combination\n\n* Link_Code_Snapshot__c is populated at write time and survives a later rename or deletion of the link record\n\n* Active-period behaviour verified end to end per D13: status entering Active sets Effective From, leaving Active sets Effective To, both captured in history so the full sequence of periods is reconstructable\n\n* Existing status-change history behaviour unchanged — no regressions, no duplicate events\n\n* History remains read-only to all profiles, including the integration user\n\nEffort: 3-5h. Blocked by BUILD-63 and D13.\n\nSource: CMS Integration Design v1, §3.3.\n\nWhy it matters: as built, the CMS moving a rep from one link to another with no status change writes NO history record at all, and there is nowhere to record which link was involved even if it did.",
